  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Task Completion Guidelines**\n\nI\'ve achieved a significant milestone! Both `lint_applet` and `compile_applet` are building perfectly, without any hitches. Now, I\'m carefully revisiting the Task Completion guidelines, ensuring I understand the final steps. I want to make sure I am providing you with the best experience possible!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully converted your Figma mockups for the campus Lost and Found application into a clean, fully responsive, and highly interactive web application utilizing React and Tailwind CSS. \n\nEvery view, element placement, color palette, and detail matches your visual mockups. The codebase is organized with robust TypeScript type definitions, modular presentation layouts, and a persistent state synchronization engine.\n\n### Key Visual and Functional Modules Built:\n\n*   **Visual Identity & Styling**:\n    *   **Typography**: Configured the elegant **Playfair Display** display font for headings alongside the clean, modern **Inter** sans-serif font for maximum readability, exactly as shown in the mockup headers and layouts.\n    *   **Color Scheme**: Applied strict contrast ratios using slate neutral tones (`bg-white` and `bg-gray-50`) paired with vibrant primary brand indicators such as **CLF blue** (`#2563EB`), **Found Item emerald** (`#00B050`), and **Lost Item red-orange** (`#EA580C`).\n\n*   **Interactive Core Views**:\n    *   **Welcome Landing Page**: Features the dual-button main call-to-action layout (\"I Lost Something\" / \"I Found Something\"), four visual statistical blocks with matching light pastel-colored backgrounds, a \"Tips for Success\" quick-reference card, and a dynamic real-time matching illustration on the right side.\n    *   **Dashboard**: Shows a scannable greeting card welcoming the user, quick-access action triggers, and a tabbed panel layout.\n        *   *My Logged Items Tab*: Renders cards representing logged reports with type tags (\"Lost\" / \"Found\"), status, locations, dates, and full descriptions.\n        *   *Matches Tab*: Aligns side-by-side matching pairs (Your Item vs. Matched Item) indicating match percentage ratings (e.g., 85% Match) and interactive buttons to coordinate returns or flag mismatches.\n    *   **Direct Message System (Chat)**: Features a split-pane communication interface with a real-time conversation search bar, conversation histories, unread counter badges, and an interactive message bubble container. \n        *   *Confirm Match Integration*: The active chat panel header displays a green \"Confirm Match\" action button that instantly transitions into a checked \"Match Confirmed\" badge on click, reflecting the status updates immediately.\n        *   *Automated Response Simulation*: When you type and send messages, mock student partners trigger natural-language replies after a brief realistic timeout, allowing you to demo the secure return flow smoothly.\n    *   **Report Entry Forms**: Developed comprehensive lost and found report fields structured in a 2-column layout (including item names, drop-down categories, description fields, location inputs, calendar dates, times, and a draggable mock file-picker area).\n    *   **Public Item Feed (Find Item)**: Built a central, searchable bulletin board where users can easily browse and filter reported items by keywords, categories, or report types.\n    *   **About Page**: Added a dedicated informational section explaining the matching logic alongside recommended safe physical exchange zones on campus.\n\n*   **Reliable State Management**:\n    *   All changes (such as reporting new items, sending messages, and confirming/rejecting matches) are saved immediately to browser `localStorage` so that your work persists across page refreshes.\n    *   Submitting a brand-new item report triggers an automatic similarity search, populating potential mock matches and animating the notification bell after 3 seconds to demonstrate the automated matching workflow.\n"
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 344553563
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
